          "source_text_sha256": "2c4a40251a2dc7a9d28bc31a41d9eba85bad4e6a5d5857620f218ecaf47c5188",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On December 24, 2015, at 6:10 PM, three people observed for 45 seconds from an apartment on the 10th floor a silent passing of a luminous object with changing colors (green, blue, orange). The object disappeared behind the building, passing over the witnesses. Only one testimony was collected. The observation of a multicolored flying object at low altitude on a holiday evening suggests a \"lighter than air\" object carried by the wind. The Orly Météociel report indicates a southwest wind, consistent with the object's movement (see the Météociel report). The multiple and changing colors point to a LED-lit balloon of a model similar to those described here. This type of festive balloon is becoming increasingly popular. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B,\" a probable observation of a LED festive balloon.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "65accb2208d6df1d3c50872488cad7a78dc87d624e655d90a3405207fc8bfd92"
        }
